I play badminton with Neha and Amit every Thursday evening.
This weekend, I invite them to my house for a meal.
I want to make a special Maharashtrian dish.
I open my laptop and search online.
I find a video of traditional Kande Pohe.
The poha looks very tasty in the picture.
I start the video and watch attentively.
In the video, the chef gives very simple instructions.
She says, "First of all, take half a kilo of thick poha."
"Then wash the poha in water and keep it aside."
I find that process very easy.
She tells the next step.
"After that, chop the onion and green chili finely."
"Heat two spoons of oil in a pan."
I remember this sequence.
First wash the poha, then chop the onion, and after that temper the spices.
This dish is absolutely perfect for my friends.
Now I start writing the market list.
